      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "57212437-f5d1-5b46-9058-006c2f9fe176",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tim McIlrath, Spike Slawson, Pete Wentz, Jay Jancetic, Daniel Binaei, Adam Bishop, Timothy Miller\n- Organizations: Arma Angelus, Rise Against, Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, Uke-Hunt, Fall Out Boy, Holy Roman Empire, Harm's Way, Racetraitor, Last Action Zeros, Mission Viejo High School, Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing\n- Places: Chicago, Mission Viejo, California, Scottsdale, Arizona\n- Products: Where Sleeplessness Is Rest from Nightmares\n- Topics: punk rock, metalcore\n\nFacts:\n- Tim McIlrath was born on November 3, 1978, and he is an American punk rock musician.\n- Spike Slawson is an American punk rock musician and a member of Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, and Uke-Hunt.\n- Arma Angelus was a Chicago metalcore band.\n- Where Sleeplessness Is Rest from Nightmares is the only studio album by Arma Angelus.\n- Pete Wentz was a vocalist in Arma Angelus and later became the bass guitarist and backing vocalist in Fall Out Boy.\n- Tim McIlrath played bass guitar in Arma Angelus and later became the lead singer of Rise Against.\n- Jay Jancetic played guitar in Arma Angelus and later played guitar for the Chicago bands Holy Roman Empire and Harm's Way.\n- Daniel Binaei was a guitarist in Arma Angelus and was formerly a member of Racetraitor.\n- Adam Bishop was a guitarist in Arma Angelus and later became an English teacher at Mission Viejo High School in Mission Viejo, California.\n- Timothy Miller played drums in Arma Angelus, later played drums for the Arizona-based punk band Last Action Zeros, and later became the owner of Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing in Scottsdale, Arizona.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d9594d42-9ebe-51a1-a688-fbb90d614b15",
        "text": "Page: Tim McIlrath. Sentence: Timothy James \"Tim\" McIlrath (born November 3, 1978) is an American punk rock musician.\nPage: Spike Slawson. Sentence: Spike Slawson is an American punk rock musician, a member of Me First and the Gimme Gimmes, Swingin' Utters, Filthy Thievin' Bastards, Re-Volts, and Uke-Hunt.\nPage: Arma Angelus. Sentence: Members of the band were Pete Wentz (vocals, now bass guitarist and backing vocalist in Fall Out Boy), Tim McIlrath (bass guitar, now lead singer of Rise Against), Jay Jancetic (guitar, last played guitar for the Chicago \"Holy Roman Empire\" and Harm's Way), Daniel Binaei (guitarist, formerly of Racetraitor), Adam Bishop (guitarist, now an English teacher at Mission Viejo High School in Mission Viejo, California) and Timothy Miller (drums, Last played drums for Arizona-based punk band Last Action Zeros & now owner of Immortal Art Tattoo & Body Piercing, located in Scottsdale, Arizona).\nPage: Where Sleeplessness Is Rest from Nightmares. Sentence: Where Sleeplessness Is Rest from Nightmares is the only studio album by the Chicago metalcore band, Arma Angelus.",
